development.key, development.crt: a key that signs the images of test
builds, and its certificate.  NOT SECRET: it is here for everyone to read,
and so proves nothing about who made an image.  A system built for
release does not take its signatures (images/system.nix: signing), and a
system that does says so of itself (VARIANT_ID=development in
/usr/lib/os-release).

The key that signs systems for release is not in this repository and is
no build's to read: tools/sign.sh asks a password manager for it when it
signs.  Its certificate is keys/verity.crt, at the top of the repository.
